{"absent":["Bodies and ordering guarantees of generic_atomic64 read, update, exchange and compare-exchange implementations.","Bodies of queued_read_lock_slowpath, queued_write_lock_slowpath, queued_spin_lock_slowpath and queued_spin_release_traced.","Definitions and semantics of hardware barrier primitives, compiler barrier, cpu_relax and arch cmpxchg.","Futex, mutex, semaphore, rwsem, percpu-rw-semaphore and other higher-level locking behavior.","Selection conditions choosing between full-barrier and compiler-only barrier configurations and pending-width variants.","Error handling, sleeping, timeout and fairness properties of contended acquisition beyond delegation to slow paths."],"dossier":"D03","findings":[{"kind":"struct","sids":["include/asm-generic/atomic64.h::atomic64_t","include/asm-generic/atomic64.h::ATOMIC64_INIT"],"text":"The 64-bit atomic type is a structure wrapping a single signed 64-bit counter aligned to its own width, with a separate initializer supplying the starting counter value."},{"kind":"struct","sids":["include/asm-generic/mcs_spinlock.h::mcs_spinlock"],"text":"The MCS queue node contains a link to the next node plus a locked flag meaning acquisition and a nesting count used by queue spin handling."},{"kind":"struct","sids":["include/asm-generic/qrwlock_types.h::qrwlock","include/asm-generic/qrwlock_types.h::arch_rwlock_t"],"text":"The queued reader-writer lock combines a shared atomic counter with a byte view exposing a write-held flag whose position depends on byte order, together with a separate queue spinlock used for waiting."},{"kind":"struct","sids":["include/asm-generic/qspinlock_types.h::qspinlock","include/asm-generic/qspinlock_types.h::arch_spinlock_t"],"text":"The queued spinlock is a union of one atomic word with byte and half-word views exposing locked and pending fields and a tail field identifying queued waiters, with field order depending on byte order."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["include/asm-generic/qrwlock.h::_QW_WAITING","include/asm-generic/qrwlock.h::_QW_LOCKED","include/asm-generic/qrwlock.h::_QW_WMASK","include/asm-generic/qrwlock.h::_QR_SHIFT","include/asm-generic/qrwlock.h::_QR_BIAS"],"text":"Reader-writer state packs a waiting-writer indication and a held-for-write value into the low nine bits, with reader count kept in higher bits as multiples of a fixed bias derived from a nine-bit shift."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["include/asm-generic/qspinlock_types.h::_Q_SET_MASK","include/asm-generic/qspinlock_types.h::_Q_LOCKED_OFFSET","include/asm-generic/qspinlock_types.h::_Q_LOCKED_BITS","include/asm-generic/qspinlock_types.h::_Q_LOCKED_MASK","include/asm-generic/qspinlock_types.h::_Q_PENDING_OFFSET","include/asm-generic/qspinlock_types.h::_Q_PENDING_BITS.alt_1","include/asm-generic/qspinlock_types.h::_Q_PENDING_BITS.alt_2","include/asm-generic/qspinlock_types.h::_Q_PENDING_MASK","include/asm-generic/qspinlock_types.h::_Q_TAIL_IDX_OFFSET","include/asm-generic/qspinlock_types.h::_Q_TAIL_CPU_OFFSET","include/asm-generic/qspinlock_types.h::_Q_TAIL_MASK","include/asm-generic/qspinlock_types.h::_Q_LOCKED_VAL","include/asm-generic/qspinlock_types.h::_Q_PENDING_VAL"],"text":"Spin state packs locked, pending and tail subfields into one 32-bit word using documented offsets and widths, with derived masks for each subfield and single-bit values for locked and pending."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["include/asm-generic/qrwlock_types.h::__ARCH_RW_LOCK_UNLOCKED","include/asm-generic/qspinlock_types.h::__ARCH_SPIN_LOCK_UNLOCKED"],"text":"The unlocked forms of both queue locks are defined as a zero counter value together with an unlocked waiter lock where applicable."},{"kind":"export","sids":["include/asm-generic/atomic64.h::ATOMIC64_OP","include/asm-generic/atomic64.h::ATOMIC64_OP_RETURN","include/asm-generic/atomic64.h::ATOMIC64_FETCH_OP","include/asm-generic/atomic64.h::ATOMIC64_OPS.alt_1","include/asm-generic/atomic64.h::ATOMIC64_OPS.alt_2"],"text":"Generic 64-bit atomics are offered in three shapes per operation: a plain update, a variant returning the new value, and a variant returning the prior value, declared through helpers parameterized by operation name."},{"kind":"export","sids":["include/asm-generic/atomic64.h::arch_atomic64_read","include/asm-generic/atomic64.h::arch_atomic64_set","include/asm-generic/atomic64.h::arch_atomic64_add","include/asm-generic/atomic64.h::arch_atomic64_sub","include/asm-generic/atomic64.h::arch_atomic64_and","include/asm-generic/atomic64.h::arch_atomic64_or","include/asm-generic/atomic64.h::arch_atomic64_xor","include/asm-generic/atomic64.h::arch_atomic64_dec_if_positive","include/asm-generic/atomic64.h::arch_atomic64_cmpxchg","include/asm-generic/atomic64.h::arch_atomic64_xchg","include/asm-generic/atomic64.h::arch_atomic64_fetch_add_unless"],"text":"The architecture layer maps its read, set, arithmetic, logic, compare-exchange, exchange, conditional decrement and conditional add-unless operations onto the corresponding generic 64-bit implementations, including a release flavoured set."},{"kind":"export","sids":["include/asm-generic/barrier.h::mb.alt_1","include/asm-generic/barrier.h::rmb.alt_1","include/asm-generic/barrier.h::wmb.alt_1","include/asm-generic/barrier.h::dma_mb.alt_1","include/asm-generic/barrier.h::mb.alt_2","include/asm-generic/barrier.h::smp_mb.alt_1","include/asm-generic/barrier.h::smp_mb.alt_2","include/asm-generic/barrier.h::virt_mb","include/asm-generic/barrier.h::virt_rmb","include/asm-generic/barrier.h::pmem_wmb","include/asm-generic/barrier.h::io_stop_wc"],"text":"Memory ordering provides full, read, write and DMA variants plus SMP-only, virtualization and persistent-memory forms, with one configuration adding sanitizer hooks around hardware primitives and another reducing SMP barriers to compiler ordering."},{"kind":"export","sids":["include/asm-generic/barrier.h::smp_cond_load_relaxed","include/asm-generic/barrier.h::smp_cond_load_acquire","include/asm-generic/barrier.h::smp_acquire__after_ctrl_dep"],"text":"Conditional spinning helpers repeatedly perform a single read until a caller predicate becomes true, with a relaxed form and an acquire form that adds ordering after the control dependency."},{"kind":"export","sids":["include/asm-generic/rwonce.h::READ_ONCE","include/asm-generic/rwonce.h::WRITE_ONCE","include/asm-generic/rwonce.h::__READ_ONCE","include/asm-generic/rwonce.h::__WRITE_ONCE","include/asm-generic/rwonce.h::READ_ONCE_NOCHECK","include/asm-generic/rwonce.h::__read_once_word_nocheck","include/asm-generic/rwonce.h::read_word_at_a_time","include/asm-generic/rwonce.h::compiletime_assert_rwonce_type"],"text":"Single-access helpers expose read-once and write-once operations with compile-time size validation, a no-check word reader, and a word-at-a-time reader that performs sanitizer checks."},{"kind":"lock","sids":["include/asm-generic/qrwlock.h::queued_read_trylock","include/asm-generic/qrwlock.h::queued_read_lock","include/asm-generic/qrwlock.h::queued_read_unlock"],"text":"Reader fast paths add the reader bias with acquire ordering and succeed only when no writer bits are present, otherwise falling back to a slow path; try-lock first samples the counter and rolls back the bias on writer interference, while unlock subtracts the bias with release ordering."},{"kind":"lock","sids":["include/asm-generic/qrwlock.h::queued_write_trylock","include/asm-generic/qrwlock.h::queued_write_lock","include/asm-generic/qrwlock.h::queued_write_unlock","include/asm-generic/qrwlock.h::queued_rwlock_is_contended"],"text":"Writer acquisition attempts an acquire compare-exchange from empty to the write-held value for the unfair case and otherwise enters a slow path; release clears only the write-held byte with release ordering, and contention is reported from the waiter spinlock state."},{"kind":"lock","sids":["include/asm-generic/qspinlock.h::queued_spin_trylock","include/asm-generic/qspinlock.h::queued_spin_lock","include/asm-generic/qspinlock.h::queued_spin_release","include/asm-generic/qspinlock.h::queued_spin_unlock"],"text":"Spin acquisition tries an acquire compare-exchange from zero to locked and otherwise enters a slow path; try-lock samples first and fails on any nonzero state, while release and unlock clear the locked byte with release ordering, optionally via a traced path when enabled."},{"kind":"lock","sids":["include/asm-generic/barrier.h::__smp_store_mb","include/asm-generic/barrier.h::__smp_mb__before_atomic","include/asm-generic/barrier.h::__smp_mb__after_atomic","include/asm-generic/barrier.h::__smp_store_release","include/asm-generic/barrier.h::__smp_load_acquire","include/asm-generic/barrier.h::smp_store_mb.alt_1","include/asm-generic/barrier.h::smp_store_release.alt_1","include/asm-generic/barrier.h::smp_load_acquire.alt_1","include/asm-generic/barrier.h::smp_store_mb.alt_2","include/asm-generic/barrier.h::smp_store_release.alt_2","include/asm-generic/barrier.h::smp_load_acquire.alt_2"],"text":"Store with barrier writes then orders, store-release orders before writing with type validation, load-acquire reads then orders, and before-or-after atomic helpers provide SMP ordering around atomic updates; one configuration reduces these to compiler barriers plus single accesses."},{"kind":"invariant","sids":["include/linux/atomic/atomic-instrumented.h::atomic_read","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic_read","include/linux/atomic/atomic-instrumented.h::atomic_add_return_acquire","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic_add_return_acquire","include/linux/atomic/atomic-instrumented.h::atomic_sub","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic_sub","include/linux/atomic/atomic-instrumented.h::atomic_sub_return_release","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic_sub_return_release","include/linux/atomic/atomic-instrumented.h::atomic_try_cmpxchg_acquire","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic_try_cmpxchg_acquire","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic_cmpxchg_acquire"],"text":"Instrumented atomic wrappers perform sanitizer accounting then delegate to raw operations, which prefer arch acquire or release variants, else combine a relaxed arch operation with an explicit fence, else use the fully ordered arch operation."},{"kind":"invariant","sids":["include/asm-generic/qspinlock.h::queued_spin_is_locked","include/asm-generic/qspinlock.h::queued_spin_value_unlocked","include/asm-generic/qspinlock.h::queued_spin_is_contended","include/asm-generic/qspinlock.h::arch_spin_is_locked","include/linux/spinlock_up.h::arch_spin_is_locked.alt_1","include/linux/spinlock_up.h::arch_spin_is_locked.alt_2"],"text":"Spin locked state is true for any nonzero word, contended state masks out the locked bits, and an unlocked-value test examines a copy; single-CPU configurations instead test a simple flag or report never locked."},{"kind":"invariant","sids":["include/asm-generic/qrwlock.h::arch_read_lock","include/asm-generic/qrwlock.h::arch_write_lock","include/asm-generic/qrwlock.h::arch_read_trylock","include/asm-generic/qrwlock.h::arch_write_trylock","include/asm-generic/qrwlock.h::arch_read_unlock","include/asm-generic/qrwlock.h::arch_write_unlock","include/asm-generic/qrwlock.h::arch_rwlock_is_contended","include/asm-generic/qspinlock.h::arch_spin_is_contended","include/asm-generic/qspinlock.h::arch_spin_lock","include/asm-generic/qspinlock.h::arch_spin_trylock","include/asm-generic/qspinlock.h::arch_spin_unlock","include/asm-generic/qspinlock.h::virt_spin_lock"],"text":"Architecture read, write and spin interfaces are direct aliases of the queued implementations, including lock, try-lock, unlock and contention queries, with an additional always-false virtualization helper."},{"kind":"state_machine","sids":["include/asm-generic/qrwlock.h::queued_read_trylock","include/asm-generic/qrwlock.h::queued_write_trylock","include/asm-generic/qrwlock.h::queued_read_lock","include/asm-generic/qrwlock.h::queued_write_lock","include/asm-generic/qrwlock.h::queued_read_unlock","include/asm-generic/qrwlock.h::queued_write_unlock"],"text":"The reader-writer counter moves between empty, reader-held counts, write-held, and writer-waiting combinations; reader bias additions that observe writer bits are unwound, and writer acquisition from empty is the only direct transition to write-held."},{"kind":"state_machine","sids":["include/asm-generic/qspinlock.h::queued_spin_trylock","include/asm-generic/qspinlock.h::queued_spin_lock","include/asm-generic/qspinlock.h::queued_spin_release","include/asm-generic/qspinlock.h::queued_spin_is_locked","include/asm-generic/qspinlock.h::queued_spin_is_contended"],"text":"The spin word moves from zero to locked on uncontended acquisition, may gain pending and tail queue state under contention handled by the slow path, and returns toward zero when the holder clears the locked portion with release ordering."},{"kind":"entry_point","sids":["include/asm-generic/qrwlock.h::queued_read_lock","include/asm-generic/qrwlock.h::queued_write_lock","include/asm-generic/qrwlock.h::queued_read_trylock","include/asm-generic/qrwlock.h::queued_write_trylock","include/asm-generic/qspinlock.h::queued_spin_lock","include/asm-generic/qspinlock.h::queued_spin_trylock","include/asm-generic/qspinlock.h::queued_spin_unlock","include/linux/atomic/atomic-instrumented.h::atomic_read","include/asm-generic/rwonce.h::READ_ONCE"],"text":"Callable entry operations in these fragments are the queued read and write lock, try-lock and unlock routines plus the queued spin lock, try-lock and unlock routines, alongside atomic read, update, compare-exchange and single-access helpers."},{"kind":"hazard","sids":["include/asm-generic/rwonce.h::read_word_at_a_time","include/asm-generic/qrwlock.h::queued_read_lock","include/asm-generic/qspinlock.h::queued_spin_unlock"],"text":"Word-at-a-time loads can race with concurrent out-of-bounds stores and must not use the stricter single-access helper; queued read slow paths own reader-count adjustment on failure; traced versus untraced spin release paths must stay behaviorally identical."},{"kind":"stub","sids":["include/linux/instrumented.h::instrument_atomic_read_write"],"text":"Stub reference to external symbol instrument_atomic_read_write."},{"kind":"stub","sids":["include/linux/instrumented.h::instrument_atomic_read"],"text":"Stub reference to external symbol instrument_atomic_read."},{"kind":"stub","sids":["include/linux/instrumented.h::instrument_read_write"],"text":"Stub reference to external symbol instrument_read_write."},{"kind":"stub","sids":["include/linux/kasan-checks.h::kasan_check_read.alt_2"],"text":"Stub reference to external symbol kasan_check_read."},{"kind":"stub","sids":["include/linux/kconfig.h::IS_ENABLED"],"text":"Stub reference to external symbol IS_ENABLED."},{"kind":"stub","sids":["include/linux/kcsan-checks.h::kcsan_check_read"],"text":"Stub reference to external symbol kcsan_check_read."},{"kind":"stub","sids":["include/linux/kcsan-checks.h::kcsan_release.alt_1"],"text":"Stub reference to external symbol kcsan_release."},{"kind":"stub","sids":["include/linux/kcsan-checks.h::kcsan_release.alt_3"],"text":"Stub reference to external symbol kcsan_release second variant."},{"kind":"stub","sids":["include/linux/tracepoint-defs.h::tracepoint_enabled.alt_1"],"text":"Stub reference to external symbol tracepoint_enabled first variant."},{"kind":"stub","sids":["include/linux/tracepoint-defs.h::tracepoint_enabled.alt_2"],"text":"Stub reference to external symbol tracepoint_enabled second variant."}],"index_id":"99dbddb713e8d299bd55ae3ea6f9df9103f2fe09352557dba05a5a735dfe6c48","lane":1,"pass":1,"prefix_sha256":"7e368f1f0746d2b5a4e6bb4196bcc8a374e26ad1af5206ff89af1d2b4c05f323","prompt_sha256":"ed9533d77d14d8b35db862d2898258c374390547d1bfc99577500878cb2e4421","schema":"lx.extract.v1","sids_read":["include/asm-generic/atomic64.h::_ASM_GENERIC_ATOMIC64_H","include/asm-generic/atomic64.h: